# Prettier is applied only to the files named in `npm run format:check`
# (package.json). Existing sources are NOT reformatted in bulk: several agents
# edit them in parallel and a repo-wide reformat would conflict with every
# open branch. These entries also keep an ad-hoc `prettier --check .` quiet on
# generated, vendored or data files.

node_modules/
package-lock.json
qa-unit-results/
qa-screenshots/
.qa-venv/

# Generated classic-script bundle: rebuilt byte-for-byte from web/assets/core-src
# by `python scripts/build_core_modules.py --write`; formatting it breaks --check.
web/assets/scripts/00-app-core.js
# Edit-time fragments of one shared IIFE (not standalone JavaScript).
web/assets/core-src/

# Data snapshots and catalogs (machine-written JSON, compared by hash/tests).
web/catalog/
web/*.json
web/assets/source-layout.json
tests/fixtures/

# Canonical documents are validated by scripts/verify_context.py hashes.
# Only the convention document written for this tooling is checked.
*.md
/docs/*
!/docs/submission/
/docs/submission/*
!/docs/submission/CODE_CONVENTION.md
